  "name": "[RMMKT] RM \u00b7 3 Enqueue Instagram post",
  "description": "",
  "active": true,
  "isArchived": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## RM \u00b7 3 \u2014 approved caption \u2192 Instagram queue\n\n**Starts:** webhook, called by the gateway when a human approves an Instagram item.\n\n**Authorised?** checks the shared token first and refuses anything else \u2014 this webhook can write to\nthe queue, so it is not open.\n\nRenders the branded card via **RM: Render Card** (a sub-workflow), then upserts a row into the\n`content_queue` data table. It does **not** post: *RM: Publish ready posts* does that on its own\nschedule, one post a day.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "overview-note",
      "name": "What this workflow does",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -40
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "rm-enqueue-instagram",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "hook",
      "name": "Webhook: gateway \u2192 enqueue",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "webhookId": "rm-enqueue-instagram",
      "notes": "Called by the gateway's /publish when a human approves an instagram item. Body: {token, tmdb_id, caption, scheduled_date, item_id, run_date}"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "token",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.token }}",
              "rightValue": "={{ $env.RM_GATEWAY_TOKEN }}"
            },
            {
              "id": "tmdb",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ String($json.body.tmdb_id ?? '') }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "cap",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.caption }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "auth",
      "name": "Authorised?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        224,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "errorMessage": "bad token, or tmdb_id/caption missing \u2014 nothing was queued"
      },
      "id": "refuse",
      "name": "Refuse",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stopAndError",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        224,
        224
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "raw",
        "jsonOutput": "={\n  \"tmdb_id\": \"{{ $json.body.tmdb_id }}\",\n  \"caption\": {{ JSON.stringify($json.body.caption) }},\n  \"scheduled_date\": \"{{ $json.body.scheduled_date || $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd') }}\",\n  \"item_id\": \"{{ $json.body.item_id || '' }}\",\n  \"run_date\": \"{{ $json.body.run_date || '' }}\"\n}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "norm",
      "name": "Normalise request",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.5,
      "position": [
        448,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "jAv1cptzC2Y8rYQA",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "passThrough"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "render",
      "name": "RM: Render Card",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        672,
        0
      ],
      "notes": "Reuses the existing branded 1080\u00d71350 card renderer (TMDB \u2192 HTML \u2192 hcti.io \u2192 public URL). Input: tmdb_id. Output: image_url, title."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict",
            "version": 2
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "img",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty",
                "singleValue": true
              },
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.image_url }}",
              "rightValue": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "rendered",
      "name": "Card rendered?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        880,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "errorMessage": "RM: Render Card returned no image_url \u2014 nothing was queued"
